{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["The reason for <b>a land of streams of water</b> is that it is like a well-watered garden — one does not irrigate it with water by foot like the land of Egypt, as it will further say (Deuteronomy 11:11), \"for it drinks water from the rain of the heavens.\" And he explained that springs and deep sources emerge in the valley and also in the mountain, and from there streams flow across it. And the verse's reading is עיינות ועיינות תהומות, like \"בעזוז עינות תהום\" (Proverbs 8:28), \"מעינות תהום רבה\" (Genesis 7:11). And the matter is that among the springs there are those that flow from the condensed moisture of the mountains — from the rains that are absorbed within them or from the vapors that rise to them — and these are what he called עיינות, like \"אל כל מעיני מים\" (I Kings 18:5), \"למעינו מים\" (Psalms 114:8). And there are among them some that emerge from the source of the deep, and these are what he called <b>תהומות</b>, that is, springs of the deep. And he said that both kinds are in the valley and also in the mountain."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:51.084355543Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}